well a las vegas woman searching for  answers this afternoon after discovering  the tree and a memorial plaque in honor  of her baby gone from a park in the lone  mountain area she spoke with with  victoria sahoo joins us live in studio  this afternoon with the next steps  victoria this mom is left devastated  because her baby was cremated and the  only place she would go to honor her  baby has suddenly disappeared and she  says the toughest part about all of this  is that no one called to give her a  warning before she found out herself  when visiting the area this weekend  this is where it was  it was like crazy what was once a  beautifully decorated plaque under a big  tree at mountain crest park is now empty  it almost felt like  something else was snatched for me again  the process of losing the baby that's an  unexpected  process on friday june 10 ambrosia crumb  came to the park to decorate the plaque  on what would have been her daughter  ava's fourth birthday only to find the  tree cut down in the plaque gone i  didn't have to find out like that on  that day i really i'm kind of  disappointed no one from the parks and  recreation department had called crump  so she doesn't know what happened or why  the memorial site was taken down after  four years vegas is hot trees die  people steal things those things happen  but i do think it could have been  handled a little differently this tree  was sentimental to crump and her family  when baby ava died they held a balloon  release near this area one balloon kind  of stayed and stuck  and we noticed it because we're like oh  that's kind of weird why is this balloon  stuck in this particular tree for so  long we kind of watched it and it  actually didn't leave until we left and  we're like well maybe she was hanging  out with us here by monday afternoon 8  news now has learned the tree was among  seven others cut down because it died  the company in charge of maintenance for  the park is called real property  management has not answered any of my  calls but they told the county they cut  down the tree a few months ago they  claimed they were backlogged which is  why they don't they didn't reach out to  the family the county says real property  management is now working with the  family to find a new memorial tree and  that baby ava's plaque has now been  recovered kirsten thank you victoria
 

